WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.680 --> 00:00:04.150
David, what do you think will happen when
Donald Trump is no longer president, whenever

00:00:04.150 --> 00:00:07.629
that is, and he loses presidential immunity
from prosecution?

00:00:07.629 --> 00:00:09.230
So I'll answer the question.

00:00:09.230 --> 00:00:13.200
Remember this whole idea of immunity?

00:00:13.200 --> 00:00:14.250
It's not been tested.

00:00:14.250 --> 00:00:20.550
It really is more of a memo that the Justice
Department has put out saying we as a policy

00:00:20.550 --> 00:00:24.340
don't believe in indicting or prosecuting
a sitting president.

00:00:24.340 --> 00:00:26.760
But here's the way that I imagine it will
go.

00:00:26.760 --> 00:00:32.129
If you were waiting around imagining that
Donald Trump is going to be criminally charged

00:00:32.129 --> 00:00:37.140
and perp walked and tried and potentially
face time in prison.

00:00:37.140 --> 00:00:38.140
Forget it.

00:00:38.140 --> 00:00:39.140
Forget it.

00:00:39.140 --> 00:00:42.350
I mean, we you know, it just doesn't happen
to presidents.

00:00:42.350 --> 00:00:44.829
Trump has violated the emoluments clause.

00:00:44.829 --> 00:00:46.600
All sorts of different financial crimes.

00:00:46.600 --> 00:00:47.950
I get it.

00:00:47.950 --> 00:00:52.020
But if you're waiting for the perp walk, I
would not hold my breath.

00:00:52.020 --> 00:00:54.140
Let's just remove Trump in November.

00:00:54.140 --> 00:00:56.720
The country and the world will be much better
for it.

00:00:56.720 --> 00:01:02.340
Now, that being said, there are active pending
criminal investigations in the southern district

00:01:02.340 --> 00:01:03.340
of New York.

00:01:03.340 --> 00:01:09.000
The New York attorney general, there is almost
no doubt whatsoever that whenever Trump's

00:01:09.000 --> 00:01:14.159
national nightmare is over and the mango menace
is gone, could be in a few months, could be

00:01:14.159 --> 00:01:19.110
in four months and a year before years and
a few months, rather.

00:01:19.110 --> 00:01:25.920
His businesses are very likely to be charged
with all sorts of criminal violations for

00:01:25.920 --> 00:01:28.580
financial improprieties.

00:01:28.580 --> 00:01:32.729
I don't imagine that Donald Trump is actually
going to take the fall or be the one who gets

00:01:32.729 --> 00:01:35.170
charged and certainly not convicted.

00:01:35.170 --> 00:01:38.590
There are likely going to be underlings that
will get plea deals.

00:01:38.590 --> 00:01:39.799
Who knows?

00:01:39.799 --> 00:01:41.010
Trump is not going to be convicted.

00:01:41.010 --> 00:01:44.910
I would be shocked if he is even charged in
those financial crimes.

00:01:44.910 --> 00:01:47.460
It's going to be financial irregularities.

00:01:47.460 --> 00:01:54.700
Could be anything from money laundering, misappropriation
of funds, all sorts of stuff like that.

00:01:54.700 --> 00:02:00.009
Now, once Trump is gone, he can be charged
with whatever a prosecutor wants to charge

00:02:00.009 --> 00:02:01.009
him with.

00:02:01.009 --> 00:02:02.009
But there is another element to this.

00:02:02.009 --> 00:02:07.270
It's not just the general reality that presidents
don't get criminally charged once they leave

00:02:07.270 --> 00:02:08.379
office.

00:02:08.379 --> 00:02:14.879
How do you get a jury that any legal system
would say is a fair one?

00:02:14.879 --> 00:02:19.299
You can't ask for a change of venue because
it was the president of the United States.

00:02:19.299 --> 00:02:25.269
You either have people who voted for the guy
on the jury who are not going to be impartial

00:02:25.269 --> 00:02:26.269
jurors.

00:02:26.269 --> 00:02:30.599
You have people who actively dislike the guy
who are not going to be impartial jurors.

00:02:30.599 --> 00:02:36.469
And even if you and I can imagine a sort of
a political person that says, listen, I didn't

00:02:36.469 --> 00:02:40.319
vote either way and I don't really pay attention
to politics.

00:02:40.319 --> 00:02:49.310
How do you actually get a at an unnamed partial
jury of Trump's peers in general as a president,

00:02:49.310 --> 00:02:52.840
but particularly when he is as polarizing
as Donald Trump has been?

00:02:52.840 --> 00:02:58.769
So I don't mean to say that this suggests
Trump has not committed crimes.

00:02:58.769 --> 00:03:02.860
I don't mean to say that Donald Trump should
not be prosecuted when he's gone.

00:03:02.860 --> 00:03:06.170
But what I am telling you is the perp walk
is not happening.

00:03:06.170 --> 00:03:11.659
The best we can hope for is that there are
some financial crimes with which Trump's businesses

00:03:11.659 --> 00:03:14.519
are charged and maybe somebody will take a
hit.

00:03:14.519 --> 00:04:23.669
We don't really.

